this["TipCustomIconsDetails"] := "Choose the icons displayed in your Quick Access Popup menu by <a>replacing the default icons</a> used by QAP with your preferred images. This tip will show you how to convert an image file to an icon (.ico) file.`n`nSee also how you can <a>manage all your menu icons</a> in one screen."
this["TipCustomIconsTitle"] := "Embellish your popup menu with your preferred icons"
this["TipCustomizeStartupDetails"] := "By default, Quick Access Popup displays the ""Customize"" window (where you can edit your menu) at startup.`n`nIf you prefer to open it only on demand, uncheck the ""Open Customize window at Startup"" checkbox in the <a>Options, Customize Window</a> dialog box.`n`nMore info in the <a>Knowledge Base</a>."
this["TipCustomizeStartupTitle"] := "Do you always want to open the QAP Customize window at startup?"
this["TipDefaultHotkeysDetails"] := "When you install it, Quick Access Popup takes control of your middle mouse button and of these keyboard shortcuts: Windows+W, Shift+Windows+W, Control+Shift+A, Control+Shift+C, Control+Shift+F and Control+Shift+U.`n`nYou can change this! Open the <a>Tools, Shortcuts</a> dialog box to remove or change these assignments.`n`nMore info in the <a>Knowledge Base</a>."
this["TipDefaultHotkeysTitle"] := "Decide which keyboard shortcuts are assigned by Quick Access Popup"
this["TipFavoriteFolderTempDetails"] := "This <a>tip on the QAP web site</a> will guide you in the steps to create a favorite to access easily your temporary work folder:`n- create a favorite for a folder;`n- give this favorite a distinct icon;`n- assign a shortcut to access it instantly.`n`nAlso see how to sync this folder's custom icon with the Windows folder."
this["TipFavoriteFolderTempTitle"] := "Create a favorite for a frequently used folder"
this["TipFolderDialogBoxDetails"] := "Changing folder inside ""Save As"" or ""Open"" dialog boxes is often described as being the single most productivity booster offered by Quick Access Popup.`n`nEnable this feature in <a>Options , General</a>.`n`nMore info in the <a>Knowledge Base</a>."
this["TipFolderDialogBoxTitle"] := "Change folder in dialog box"
this["TipInTheWorksDetails"] := "The ""In the Works"" menu shows what you work on actually or what content you use frequently.`n`nSee <a>what is the ""In the Works""</a> menu and its ""Frequent"", ""Recent"" and ""Current Windows"" menus and understand how these menus are built."
this["TipInTheWorksTitle"] := "What is the ""In the Works"" menu?"
this["TipMenuTriggersDetails"] := "You can open the Quick Access Popup menu using various mouse buttons or keyboard shortcuts.`n`nConfigure these triggers in <a>Options, Popup Hotkeys</a>. You can also open it from the Windows Explorer context menus.`n`nSee this page in the <a>Knowledge Base</a> and this video showing <a>12 ways to popup your QAP menu</a>."
this["TipMenuTriggersTitle"] := "Various ways to popup your favorites menu"
this["TipSearchFavoritesDetails"] := "As your menu grows, see how you can quickly <a>locate favorites in your submenus</a>.`n`nIn addition to easing favorites edition, this tool also gives you a global view of your favorites, allowing to eliminate unwanted duplicates or to better organize your menu."
